mittleff - Mittleff C Library
================================

A professional, distributable shared library built with autotools, demonstrating
best practices for C library development.

Version: 0.1 (Pre-release)
License: MIT
Author: Victor P. Santos


FEATURES
--------

* Shared and static library builds
* Namespaced header installation (mittleff/mittleff.h)
* pkg-config support for easy integration
* Symbol visibility control for clean ABI
* Comprehensive API documentation
* Unit tests using Check framework
* Example programs included
* Full autotools build system


REQUIREMENTS
------------

Build Requirements:
  - C compiler (GCC, Clang, etc.)
  - GNU Autotools (autoconf, automake, libtool)
  - pkg-config
  - Check framework >= 0.9.4 (for tests)

Runtime Requirements:
  - Standard C library


BUILDING FROM SOURCE
--------------------

1. If building from git (not from a release tarball), first run:

   $ autoreconf -fi

2. Configure the build:

   $ ./configure

   Common configure options:
   --prefix=/usr/local     Installation prefix (default: /usr/local)
   --enable-shared         Build shared libraries (default: yes)
   --enable-static         Build static libraries (default: yes)
   --disable-shared        Build only static libraries
   --disable-static        Build only shared libraries

3. Build the library:

   $ make

4. Run the test suite:

   $ make check

5. Install (may require root/sudo):

   $ make install

   Or to a staging directory:

   $ make install DESTDIR=/tmp/staging


BUILDING A DISTRIBUTION TARBALL
-------------------------------

To create a distributable source tarball:

  $ make dist

This creates mittleff-0.1.tar.gz

To verify the distribution is complete and builds correctly:

  $ make distcheck


INSTALLATION LAYOUT
-------------------

After installation, files are placed as follows:

  ${prefix}/lib/
    libmittleff.so.0.0.0       Shared library
    libmittleff.so.0           SONAME symlink
    libmittleff.so             Development symlink
    libmittleff.a              Static library
    libmittleff.la             Libtool library
    pkgconfig/mittleff.pc     pkg-config file

  ${prefix}/include/mittleff/
    mittleff.h                 Public header

  ${prefix}/share/doc/mittleff/
    README, AUTHORS, NEWS, ChangeLog, COPYING


USING THE LIBRARY
-----------------

Include the header in your C code:

    #include <mittleff/mittleff.h>

    int main(void) {
        int result = hello();
        return 0;
    }

Compile with pkg-config (recommended):

    $ gcc -o myapp myapp.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs mittleff)

Or manually specify flags:

    $ gcc -o myapp myapp.c -I/usr/local/include -L/usr/local/lib -lmittleff

For more examples, see the examples/ directory.


API DOCUMENTATION
-----------------

The library currently provides:

  int hello(void)
    Prints a hello message with library version information.
    Returns: 5

For detailed API documentation, see the header file:
  /usr/local/include/mittleff/mittleff.h


RUNNING TESTS
-------------

The test suite uses the Check framework. Run tests with:

  $ make check

To run tests with verbose output:

  $ make check VERBOSE=1


UNINSTALLING
------------

To remove installed files:

  $ make uninstall


VERSIONING
----------

This library follows semantic versioning principles:
  - Version 0.x indicates pre-release/unstable API
  - API may change between 0.x versions
  - Version 1.0 will mark the first stable API release

The library uses libtool versioning (version-info):
  - Current: 0 - API interface number
  - Revision: 0 - Implementation revision
  - Age: 0 - Number of backward-compatible interfaces


